I agree with Philip's interpretation of the source - the armour itself has to
provide disintegration resistance (or reflection), or it will be destroyed:

      if (uarms && !(EReflecting & W_ARMS) &&
          !(EDisint_resistance & W_ARMS))
    (void) destroy_arm(uarms);
      if (uarmc && !(EReflecting & W_ARMC) &&
          !(EDisint_resistance & W_ARMC))
    (void) destroy_arm(uarmc);
      if (uarm && !(EReflecting & W_ARM) &&
          !(EDisint_resistance & W_ARM) && !uarmc)
    (void) destroy_arm(uarm);
#ifdef TOURIST
      if (uarmu && !uarm && !uarmc) (void) destroy_arm(uarmu);
#endif

EReflecting and EDisint_resistance are sets of flags indicating the
source(s) of the player's extrinsic protection.


